21|0@TrollXChromosomes^1440118964#cua5qif:CordycepsFungus$:yeah I suppose you're right, but it can get tricky with language, you know? I mean I could say "I'm so lame" but then again I have a friend who actually has nerve damage in their left arm so they can't use it that well, so maybe I shouldn't be using that word either? Or what about moron, which has the same etymology as retard, where to we draw the line here? And in a developmental sense, the fact that I regressed to a state where I literally couldn't swallow, I was technically retarded in its truest linguistic sense, if you think about it. I can tell this would upset some people and I get why, but I feel like this one's kind of not as bad or serious as "fag/gay" or the n-word. Or at the very least it's much more of a grey area.
